# File: scripts/__tests__/upgrade-test-layers.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/572-add-an-sdlc-upgrade-project-item-that-migrates-non-kept-test-layers-into-bdd-scenarios-under-a-coverage-guarantee/requirements.md
Feature: Add an /sdlc-upgrade-project item that migrates non-kept test layers into BDD scenarios under a coverage guarantee

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Operator chooses kept test types
    Given a project with bdd and unit test files
    When /sdlc-upgrade-project runs interactively
    Then one multi-select question lists only bdd and unit, with bdd first and recommended
    And the approved apply with --kept bdd,unit writes {"version":1,"kept":["bdd","unit"]} to steering/test-layers.json

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Non-interactive run without a recorded choice changes nothing
    Given no steering/test-layers.json
    When sdlc-upgrade.mjs detect runs and apply runs with the test-layers id but no --kept
    Then the test-layers item is listed as a proposal
    And apply reports skipped:kept_types_unrecorded
    And no test or steering file changes

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: Duplicate layers are detected only for non-kept types
    Given steering/test-layers.json keeps <kept>
    And a valid steering/test-coverage.json
    When test-layers-candidates runs
    Then <outcome>

    Examples:
      | kept           | outcome                                                                     |
      | ["bdd"]        | the paired unit file and the coverage-subset unit test are candidates       |
      | ["bdd","unit"] | no unit test is a candidate                                                 |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Fully duplicated tests are deleted with evidence
    Given a unit test whose lines, branches and outcomes are a subset of one bdd test's
    When its batch begins, the test is deleted, and the batch is gated
    Then the batch is accepted
    And the evidence records the test, the covering bdd test, and the covered lines

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Uncovered behavior is converted before deletion
    Given a paired unit test that covers an outcome no scenario covers
    When its batch adds an Examples row to the paired feature covering that outcome and deletes the unit test
    Then the gate accepts the batch

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Coverage gap refuses the batch
    Given a batch that deletes a unit test whose outcome no kept-type test covers afterwards
    When the batch is gated
    Then it is refused with test_layers_coverage_gap listing the uncovered lines, branches and outcomes
    And the project is byte-identical to its pre-batch state

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Red suite refuses the batch
    Given a batch after which the suite command exits non-zero
    When the batch is gated
    Then it is refused with test_layers_suite_failed
    And the project is byte-identical to its pre-batch state

  @SCN008
  Scenario Outline: Missing coverage command refuses deletion
    Given steering/test-coverage.json is <state>
    When apply runs with --kept bdd and test-layers-candidates runs
    Then steering/test-layers.json and the inventory are recorded
    And no batch is offered and the refusal is <reasonCode> naming steering/test-coverage.json

    Examples:
      | state                     | reasonCode                    |
      | missing                   | test_coverage_command_missing |
      | {"version":2}             | test_coverage_config_invalid  |

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Before/after report
    Given a migration with one accepted and one refused batch
    When test-layers-report runs
    Then it prints before and after testCount, wallMs, lines, branches and outcomes
    And it lists the refused batch with its gap
    And no after-coverage count is lower than its before count

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Choice can be changed by rerunning
    Given steering/test-layers.json keeps bdd and unit
    When apply reruns with --kept bdd
    Then the file keeps only bdd
    And unit tests become migration candidates
